To deliver this project, we will leverage our expertise in Large Language Models (LLMs) and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities. Our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, will be fine-tuned using our established methods such as LoRA, QLoRA, or full fine-tuning on a domain-specific corpus to improve its performance in the context of administrative tasks.

Our innovation strategy will be centered around our current research topics, including knowledge graphs for procedural reasoning and multi-agent collaboration frameworks. We will also ensure that our solution complies with regulatory requirements, such as the EU AI Act, and adheres to our established bias testing process, which includes quarterly evaluations on demographically diverse test sets.

In terms of environmental sustainability, we have partnered with green hosting providers, such as OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France, which use 100% renewable energy and have low power usage effectiveness (PUE) ratings. Our digital sobriety practices include INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle.

